author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "The MCP default mutation echo matches the CLI default in both content and size, so neither surface requires a flag to obtain the lean form; The result wrapper divergence is resolved or documented as a protocol requirement with one accessor path stated for agents parsing both surfaces; A test asserts the byte-size relationship between the two surfaces for a representative mutation, so the ratio cannot silently invert again; The parity claim in the closed pm-nilh is corrected by a comment on that item pointing at this one, so the closed record does not continue to assert a parity that HEAD does not have; The measured CLI 72 bytes versus MCP 373 bytes baseline is recorded, and the post-fix numbers are reported against it"
parent: pm-5k4v
risk: medium
confidence: 96
resolution: Aligned raw SDK and MCP mutation defaults with the CLI lean envelope while preserving explicit fullChangedFields output and documenting protocol framing.
expected_result: An identical create returns the same lean envelope on both surfaces without a flag.
actual_result: An isolated identical create returns id/status/changed_field_count at 57 bytes on both CLI and MCP result; fullChangedFields restores the full envelope.
