comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-01T00:35:37.291Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence 2026-08-01: raw SDK/MCP mutation actions create, copy, update, close, append, and restore now use the same lean id/status/changed_field_count default as the CLI, while typed PmClient convenience methods preserve full results through explicit fullChangedFields opt-in. Isolated identical creates measured 57 bytes on both CLI and MCP result versus the recorded 72/373-byte baseline. The MCP JSON-RPC structuredContent.result protocol wrapper remains documented, but both surfaces expose the same keys inside the result. Focused parity tests passed 22/22; the repo-wide suite passed 6631/6631 at 100/100/100/100 coverage."
  "2026-08-01T01:10:10.295Z","harness:codex","PR #849 exact-head CI correction: the Claude plugin smoke was the remaining consumer of the retired verbose raw pm_create result. It now requires the exact lean id/status/changed_field_count key set and a non-empty id; unit tests reject both verbose and malformed envelopes. Focused tests passed 19/19, the real MCP/plugin smoke passed all 31 tools and its full workflow, and ESLint passed."
